'''bamalipton''' (bam-ạ-lip′tọn), ''n.'' [An artificial term.] A mood of syllogism, differing from baralipton only in having the names of the major and minor premises transposed. {{smaller|The name was invented by Jodoc Trutfeder of Eisenach, a teacher of Luther, who died in 1519.}}

'''bambara''' (bam′bạ-rä), ''n.'' [An artificial term.] A mood of syllogism, differing from barbara only in having the names of the major and minor premises transposed. The name was invented by Jodoc Trutfeder. See ''bamalipton''.

